  "description": "A parametric TRACK on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nDROP IT ON A SEGMENT. It is the rail, not the light: `track-head` is the fitting, and it carries the lamp.\n\nTHE HEADS ARE LAID OUT FROM ONE END, the way a rail is actually loaded, and squeezed if they would run off it. `spacingUsed` and `spacingSqueezed` say which happened. Reporting the spacing that was used rather than the one that was asked for is the difference between a layout and a wish.\n\nWHAT THE RAIL OWNS IS THE CIRCUIT. A 16 A 230 V circuit is 3680 W; ten 50 W heads on it is 14 %, and thirty 150 W heads is 122 %, which is the one failure mode this object exists to catch. A magnetic 48 V track fails it far sooner, which is exactly why the supply is a parameter rather than an assumption.\n\nIT HAS NO LAMP BLOCK. A rail is infrastructure. Giving it lumens would mean every head on it double-counted.\n\nDIMENSIONS AT THE DEFAULTS: a 3 m surface rail at 2.7 m with three heads at 800 mm from 400 mm in, 15 W on a 3680 W circuit — 0.4 %.",
